  helper. It intentionally carries the same context as review.user plus the
  selected axis label.
*/ -}}
{{- define "implementation_review_axis.user" -}}
Axis under review: {{ .AxisLabel }}
{{ if .GateLabel }}Gate under review: {{ .GateLabel }}
{{ end -}}
Review feedback output: {{ .FeedbackPath }}

Iteration under review: {{ .Iteration }}
Iteration artifacts directory: {{ .IterDir }}

{{ if or .DesignArtifactPath .FeatureDescription }}## Approved Design Grounding

{{ if .DesignArtifactPath }}Approved design: {{ .DesignArtifactPath }}

{{ end }}{{ if .FeatureDescription }}Approved intent:
{{ .FeatureDescription }}

{{ end }}{{ end -}}
{{ if .LiveRunAxis }}## Live-Run Posture

- Use the live-run posture: build, launch, run, drive, screenshot, and record evidence as needed.
- Treat the source tree as read-only. Write captured evidence only under the live-run evidence root named in this prompt.
- For visual judgments, use the attached baseline images plus the screenshots captured for the plan's verification under the implementation iteration directories.

{{ else }}## Review Posture

- Keep this axis read-only: inspect source and artifacts, then write only the required review-feedback.md file.

{{ end -}}
{{ if .RefactorPassForkPoint }}## Refactor Pass Fork Point

This feature is a refactor pass forked from its parent feature's delivered state at {{ .RefactorPassForkPoint }}. The cumulative diff therefore also contains the parent's approved, already-delivered changes: anything that already exists at the fork point belongs to the parent, not to this pass. Wherever the specification refers to prior, current, or existing state, resolve that reference against the fork point — this pass's own delta is `git diff <fork-sha>..HEAD` — never against the repository base branch. Judge the assembled result as a whole, but attribute each change to the record that made it: the parent's delivered state is not, by itself, a finding against this pass. All work is confined to the worktrees listed for this pass: other checkouts of the same repositories exist and are off-limits.

{{ end -}}
{{ if .FinalGate }}## Final Review Scope

Review the assembled feature across the cumulative cross-repo diff.
{{ if .DiffBase }}Cumulative diff base: {{ .DiffBase }}
{{ end }}
Scope guidance:
- Judge the whole assembled feature across all repositories in the workspace.
- Use the approved roadmap as scope context for the completed feature, not as a reason to ignore feature-level gaps.
- The whole feature is in scope at Final Review, including work no single phase covered.
{{ if .RoadmapPath }}Read the approved roadmap at: {{ .RoadmapPath }}

{{ end }}{{ if .PlanPath }}Read the implementation plan at: {{ .PlanPath }}

{{ end }}{{ else if .RoadmapPath }}## Approved Roadmap

This phase is one step in a larger plan. Read the approved roadmap at: {{ .RoadmapPath }}

Scope guidance:
- Your review MUST be scoped to the current phase's objectives only.
- Consult the roadmap to understand what this phase is responsible for and what later phases will handle.
- Do NOT flag missing functionality that is explicitly deferred to a subsequent phase in the roadmap.
- Do NOT request changes for incomplete features that are scheduled for later phases.
- DO flag issues where this phase's specific objectives are not met.

{{ end }}{{ if and (not .FinalGate) .PlanPath }}## Implementation Plan

Read the implementation plan (source of truth) at: {{ .PlanPath }}

{{ end }}{{ if .AcceptanceClause }}## Acceptance

{{ .AcceptanceClause }}

{{ end }}{{ if .ExitCriteria }}## Exit Criteria

{{ .ExitCriteria }}

{{ end }}{{ if .ProgressPath }}## Progress

Read the current progress at: {{ .ProgressPath }}

{{ end }}{{ if and (not .FinalGate) .PhaseType }}## Phase Type

This is a **{{ .PhaseType }}** phase. If the axis methodology defines phase-aware criteria, apply them; otherwise use the phase type as scope context.
{{ end }}{{- end -}}
